  "discrepancy_investigation": "In earlier draft material, a hardcoded summary template cited '0.40 \u00b5s' for Cost-Optimal and '21.28 \u00b5s' for DQN. However, actual microbenchmarking on Python 3.14 (CPU) across 10,000 timed flow observations with 1,000 warmup steps measured: Cost-Optimal median = 1.95 \u00b5s (policy-only), 45.26 \u00b5s (E2E). DQN median = 100.23 \u00b5s (policy-only), 159.68 \u00b5s (E2E). The 0.40 \u00b5s figure arose from an un-sanitized prototype script that omitted input validation and tie-breaking.",
